<title>USA: Nutrition/Life Q1 Dec 31 loss.</title>
<headline>Nutrition/Life Q1 Dec 31 loss.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>NUTRITION FOR LIFE INTERNATIONAL, INC.</p>
<p>		  Condensed Consolidated Statements of Operations</p>
<p>			 (in thousands except per share data)</p>
<p>							 Three Months Ended</p>
<p>								December 31,</p>
<p>						     1996	     1995</p>
<p> Sales					   $19,269	  $21,262</p>
<p> Cost of sales				  14,185	   14,492</p>
<p>Marketing, distribution and administrative expenses</p>
<p>						     5,580	    2,902</p>
<p>   Operating income (loss)		   (496)	    3,868</p>
<p> Other income (expense)		    (6,281)		132</p>
<p> Income (loss) before income tax expense benefit(6,777) 4,000</p>
<p> Income tax expense (benefit)	    (2,281)	    1,447</p>
<p>   Net income (loss)			 (4,496)	    2,553</p>
<p>Earnings (loss) per common share:</p>
<p> Primary					   (.71)		.40</p>
<p> Fully diluted				   (.71)		.39</p>
<p>Weighted average shares outstanding</p>
<p>						 6,319,813	6,419,365</p>
<p>Fully diluted weighted average shares</p>
<p>  outstanding				6,319,813	6,555,085</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 Q1 loss includes $6.4 million expenses accrued to account for costs related to the preliminary settlement of class action suits filed against the company in 1996. A related income tax benefit of $2.2 million has also been recognized.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
